## `Limited by` definitions

Items are bought one reprocessing portion at a time, cheapest sell order first.
`Limited by` names the condition that stopped the next portion, so `Buy units` is the
largest quantity that remained worthwhile.

| Value | Meaning | What to do |
| ----- | ------- | ---------- |
| input supply exhausted | Every hub sell order for the item was bought; fewer than one more portion remains on the market. | The whole listed supply is profitable. Watch for restocks. |
| marginal portion not profitable | The next portion would cost more than its materials return after fees, or its margin would fall below the minimum margin ({{ number(options.min_margin) }}%). Usually the next input sell order is too expensive or, in the immediate table, material buy orders have been walked down to lower prices. | Stop at `Buy units`; buying more loses money or falls below the threshold. |
| `<material>` buy depth exhausted | Immediate table only. Selling the next portion's materials would need more of that material than the hub buy orders hold. | The market cannot absorb more of this material now. Sell the rest later or list it instead. |
| capped at {{ max_portions }} portions | A safety limit on the purchase walk was reached before any other condition. | Deal size is understated; check the market directly. |

The sell-order table prices materials at a fixed 5% sell price with no depth limit, so
it is only stopped by input supply or the input price. Use the `exceeds_daily_volume`
flag to judge whether the listings would actually sell.
